# Deliberately minimal scope - not a global `* text=auto`, which would
# trigger a repo-wide renormalization diff on first checkout (RESEARCH.md
# Pitfall 5). These two rules declare only the paths whose line endings must
# be byte-stable across a local Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) and
# the ubuntu-latest CI/release runner, so `git diff --exit-code dist/` after
# a rebuild is deterministic rather than a false-positive from CRLF drift.
dist/** -text
*.ttf -text
